{"input": "What did Huw Irranca-Davies think about the capacity in the next several years to deliver the product when talking about childcare offer?", "answers": ["Huw Irranca-Davies thought there would be capacity growth in the next two to three years to deliver the product. The confidence was constructed by the development of roll-out, in which the team was learning live time. Moreover, there was a separate fund into cycle meithrin to address the issue of the Welsh language."], "length": 12342, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Huw Irranca-Davies expressed confidence that there would be capacity growth in the next two to three years to deliver the childcare offer, citing the work being done on the ground with the phased roll-out, weekly or fortnightly updates, and a termly update, as well as feedback from childcare providers that they can meet the demand with the right support and funding."}
{"input": "What did the User Interface think about their previous suggestions when discussing the user interface?", "answers": ["The User Interface affirmed their previous efforts at first, but he thought that was not enough, so he went on to propose that they might consider buying another face plate and include a touch screen. In terms of the buttons on the screen, the User Interface found the existing problem that some of the buttons would be stuck in the screen and not so easy to be found and touched, so he suggested making those essential buttons in conspicuous colours like red."], "length": 7881, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The User Interface designer, Ron, thought that some of the previous suggestions they had made, such as the touch screen interface and the jumbo universal remote control, were not what the team was going for, but they also thought that some of the ideas they had come up with, such as the voice recognition and the use of recognizable colors and shapes, were good ideas and worth considering."}
{"input": "Why did the group think of the locator when presenting the functional requirements?", "answers": ["When Marketing mentioned about the long battery life, the group came up with the locator that the remote could beep when users clapped. Also, this function should be designed to not beep every five minutes so that users would not like the remote. The group mates agreed on it and thought it was an interesting and excellent idea."], "length": 8489, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group thought of the locator as a feature for the remote control because it would be similar to a mobile phone locator, allowing users to easily find the remote control if it was misplaced. Marketing suggested this idea, saying \"like you have for a mobile phone or not a mobile phone, some kind of a ring, keys and things like that, so maybe something where you clap and then it beeps, something a kind of sound that you don't often hear on the T_V_\"."}
{"input": "Summarize what was said about the microphone data", "answers": ["The group discussed recognition results generated for 20 minutes of close-talking microphone data. Recognition performance was very good, indicating promising results for forced alignment procedures and the ability to analyze other important signal information, e.g. prosody and overlapping speech. It was decided that close-talking data should be downsampled and fed to the SRI recognizer to compare recognition performance, and that data from the far-field microphones should be tested on the recognizer as soon as possible."], "length": 12786, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed the microphone data, specifically the downsampling of the audio files from 48 kHz to 16 kHz, which was done to make the files smaller and easier to transfer. It was mentioned that the downsampling was already being done, and that the original 48 kHz files were being downsampled to 16 kHz before being used for recognition. The group also discussed the possibility of trying to use the original 48 kHz files without downsampling, and the potential benefits and drawbacks of doing so. Additionally, the group talked about the possibility of using a different type of microphone, such as a hand-held microphone, and the potential benefits and drawbacks of doing so."}
{"input": "What did the user interface designer propose in the discussion about industrial components?", "answers": ["Although the industrial designer regarded LCD as costly, the user interface designer proposed adding an LCD as a kind of output that only displayed some information or menu and was not touch sensitive, which might reduce the cost."], "length": 6961, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The user interface designer proposed using a simple battery instead of solar cells, and a titanium design instead of rubber, citing cost and manufacturing issues as reasons. They also suggested using push buttons instead of a liquid crystal display (LCD) for the user interface, as it would be less expensive and easier to manufacture."}
{"input": "What did Huw Irranca-Davies think about the affordability of lowest-income working families when talking about hourly rates of the service?", "answers": ["Huw Irranca-Davies thought £4.50amount was an appropriate and universal amount. As for the add-ons, even low-income families could discriminate between providers. Also, the team would be substantially transparent thus parents can make the decisions."], "length": 12340, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Huw Irranca-Davies acknowledged that the hourly rate of £4.50 might not be sufficient for lowest-income working families, particularly in areas with higher costs of living, and that they might be unduly affected by additional charges for services such as food, snacks, and transport. However, he also emphasized that the £4.50 rate was a contribution towards the wraparound childcare element and that parents were used to making decisions about additional costs with childcare providers, and that the scheme was designed to be affordable within the constraints of the Welsh Government's budget."}
{"input": "What did the group discuss about the design goal of the remote control?", "answers": ["They wanted it to be original, trendy, user-friendly, durable, creative and characteristic, so it can be very intuitive that people could use the product. In addition, the price, cost and expected profit of the remote control were also determined. In the part of creativity, they pointed out that creativity should have its own characteristics and ensure its fashion without affecting its functionality, so as to truly \"introduce fashion into electronics\". In terms of function, it is necessary to simplify the switch and guarantee function."], "length": 3976, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group discussed the design goal of the remote control, aiming to create a product that is original, trendy, and user-friendly, with a focus on making it intuitive and easy to use. They also brainstormed ideas for unique features that would set the remote control apart from existing ones, such as a menu-based interface, minimal buttons, and a sleek and stylish design."}
{"input": "How would the allocation contribute to educational research?", "answers": ["To start with, Bethan Owen first pointed out that figures showed that the percentage of income that had come from research in Wales was smaller than that in England, so the Welsh universities were receiving less of the money that was available, which was a factor that resulted from having less QR as a percentage. To tackle this issue, the government had provided funding in 2017-18 and 2018-19 to WISERD Education, which was a research collaboration between a number of the Welsh universities, specifically looking at educational issues. However, it was still early to see how allocation for 2019-20 would work."], "length": 10200, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The allocation for 2019-20 would contribute to educational research through funding provided to WISERD Education, a research collaboration between several Welsh universities, specifically looking at educational issues, and additional funding to add value to the Welsh Government's existing evaluation of the progress of pioneer schools in developing the three-to-15 curriculum in Wales."}
{"input": "What's the decision of remote feature design?", "answers": ["Project Manager believed that it could not be heavy. Industrial Designer indicated that fewer and bigger buttons are better and should be bust-free, for instance, rubber could be used on it. Industrial Designer also suggested that when users push a button, they could hear some sort of bleep. User Interface suggested a LED on the corner and not too expensive material like plastic could be used. Marketing added that it should look nice for better sales and should work with as many as possible of existing products listed on their website. Industrial Designer also concluded that it should be battery-saving."], "length": 1789, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team decided to design a remote control with a simple and user-friendly interface, featuring big buttons, a LED indicator to show battery life, and a design that is not too heavy and durable to prevent breakage. They also discussed the importance of making it compatible with multiple devices and not requiring frequent battery changes."}
{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["This meeting is about some final decisions on the design of the remote control. It started with presentations on the conceptual design from Marketing, Industrial Designer, and User Interface, and had a discussion on the decisions about the control. The Project Manager put a file in his folder to place the kind of decisions they should take."], "length": 11169, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was a discussion among a project manager, an industrial designer, a marketing representative, and a user interface designer to design a new remote control for a product. They discussed various aspects of the design, including the material, shape, color, and functionality of the remote. They decided on a titanium back and a plastic front, with a curved shape and a fruity color scheme. They also discussed the user interface, including the placement of buttons, the use of an LCD screen, and the implementation of voice recognition technology. Additionally, they talked about the trend-watching aspect of the design, including the use of bright colors and the launch of different packages with various front designs. The meeting concluded with the team deciding to work together to create a prototype design, with the industrial designer and user interface designer working on the design and the project manager overseeing the project."}
{"input": "Summarize the decision of the discussion about the design goal of the remote control.", "answers": ["The group hoped that it can be applied to children, in particular to ensure their safety during use. Besides, it should be colourful and beautiful to attract the attention of children. The price also should be reasonable and affordable, not too expensive, but the profit can be guaranteed. In terms of function design, unnecessary functions and switches should be removed to enhance their applicability."], "length": 3239, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The design goal of the remote control is to create a user-friendly, original, and trendy device that is functional, conceptual, and detailed in its design. The team aims to make it robust, waterproof, and baby-proof, with a simple and intuitive interface that is easy to use, even for children. The remote control should be small and compact, with a limited number of buttons, and possibly have a universal design that can be used for multiple devices. The team also discussed the idea of making the remote control adaptable to different users, such as left- or right-handed individuals, and possibly incorporating a screen or a brain-controlled interface. However, these ideas were not fully developed or agreed upon during the meeting."}
{"input": "How did Eluned Morgan respond to whether wishing to see people have greater pay equality between schoolteachers and FE when discussing the pay dispute situation?", "answers": ["Eluned Morgan said that they would wish to see pay equality in relation to teaching. As for whether all staff should get the increase or only teaching staff but not non-teaching staff, Eluned Morgan thought this should be up to ColegauCymru to negotiate and to discuss, and they should wait for their outcomes."], "length": 13887, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Eluned Morgan stated that in relation to teaching, she thinks it's fair to say that the Welsh Government would wish to see pay equality, but when asked if this would also apply to non-teaching staff, she said \"let's see\" and that it's up to ColegauCymru to negotiate and discuss."}
{"input": "Summarize the review of some problems from the past meetings.", "answers": ["The group briefly talked about their agreements of the past meetings. They were all concerned with the interchangeable user interfaces and they agreed to make it more natural-looking and multi-faces. The Industrial Design then mentioned the issue of the material. They decided to use a rubber coat in case the remote control would be damaged when being dropped occasionally. After most details were checked, the Project Manager turned to the budget problem. It is quite essential for them to be both environmentally friendly and economic."], "length": 9188, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed some problems from past meetings, including the lack of information provided to them, which made it difficult to plan and prepare for the project. They also mentioned that the level of information dropped off severely over the course of the day, and that they didn't receive any information for the last presentation. Additionally, they noted that the team's discussion often centered around the User Interface's task, which was the main focus of the project."}
{"input": "What did the group think of disposable income when discussing general requirements?", "answers": ["Industrial Designer suggested they should also look up popularity among the 25 to 35 years old age group if they looked into a stylish design. Marketing said it was 70% popular among this age group and thought this age group didn't have much economic burden so the remote price should not be unaffordable. User Interface supplemented that their remote might not function with the old TV. Therefore, the group decided to include both 15 to 25 and 25 to 35 years old age group into consideration."], "length": 8488, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group discussed that younger people, particularly those between 15-25 years old, have a higher disposable income due to not having commitments such as mortgages, life insurance policies, and cars, making them more likely to spend money on a stylish remote control."}
{"input": "What is the conclusion of the discussion about Marketing strategy when discussing group's plan of their marketing strategy?", "answers": ["The team decided that the remote had to be compatible with most of the world's TVS, or at least the ones they made. And the buttons must be internationally recognized.They also thought that the function of the remote control was to change the state of the TV and this could be realized by pressing the button."], "length": 6395, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The conclusion of the discussion about marketing strategy is that the group plans to make their remote control universal, compatible with various brands and devices, and trendy, with the possibility of customizing it with different colors or special paint jobs. They also discussed the importance of making it user-friendly and easy to learn, with a focus on international recognition and consistency with other devices."}
{"input": "Why did the marketing think they should aim at young people?", "answers": ["Because in general the early adopters of a new device were young people and teletext was used less among the young than the elderly. Plus, the young found it very relevant to have speech recognition in their remote control so that they could just tell the controller what they wanted instead of zapping."], "length": 7341, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The marketing expert, Sammy Benjo, thought they should aim at young people because they are the early adopters of new devices and are more likely to be interested in a new remote control. Additionally, young people are more likely to use features such as speech recognition, which was mentioned as a potential feature for the new remote control."}
{"input": "Summarize the discussion about the early implementer areas.", "answers": ["Huw Irranca-Davies said the process of early implementer areas had gone well and were encouraged to expand. Two things had been learned during this process by their team. To respond to the questioner, Huw Irranca-Davies then further explained the administrative burden they met and expressed a confident attitude in addressing that. The next question answered was about the spread issue of this project."], "length": 12328, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Minister for Children and Social Care, Huw Irranca-Davies, discussed the early implementer areas, stating that the childcare offer has gone well, but with some challenges, including bureaucracy and communication issues. He mentioned that the administrative burden on local authorities is significant, particularly in terms of proving eligibility and dealing with changing work patterns. The Minister also highlighted the need to learn from the early implementer areas, including the expansion of the offer to new areas, such as Gwynedd, Anglesey, and Caerphilly, and the introduction of a centralized system, similar to HMRC, to simplify the process. He expressed confidence that the lessons learned from the early implementer areas will inform the wider roll-out of the childcare offer by 2020."}
{"input": "What did Julie Morgan elaborate on the online survey when talking about the evaluations on the legitimacy of the children's rights, protection and demands?", "answers": ["When discussing the evaluations on the legitimacy of the children's rights, protection and demands, Julie Morgan mentioned that they had carried out an online survey to look into the children's thoughts and demands over the pandemic.The survey involved what did the children do through the lockdown, what they thought about the measures that Welsh government and their schools had taken, and whether they were looking for the reschooling. With those questions, the group was meant to have a more overall idea of the children's rights and demands in order to care for them better during this period."], "length": 10510, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Julie Morgan explained that the Welsh Government is launching an online survey next week to gather the views of children on the COVID-19 situation, in collaboration with the children's commissioner, Young Wales, and the Youth Parliament. This survey aims to understand the impact of the pandemic on children, their experiences, and their perceptions of the Welsh Government's response, with the goal of gathering feedback from thousands of children to inform future policy and decision-making."}
{"input": "Summarize discussion about the desired features of remote control.", "answers": ["The team came up with some general desired features about their new TV remote controls,including compatibility, appearance and functions .First, they thought compatibility is of importance.Second ,they thought good looks and sizes of remote controls were two vital features .Third, buttons should be designed properly."], "length": 6386, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed various features of the remote control, including its design, functionality, and usability. They agreed that it should be original and trendy, with a shape that fits comfortably in the hand, and a layout that is easy to use and understand. The remote should have a universal design that works with different brands and systems, and should be compatible with devices such as D_V_D_ players and televisions. They also discussed the importance of having a simple and intuitive interface, with clear and recognizable buttons, and the possibility of using colors and custom designs to make the remote more appealing. Additionally, they mentioned the need for the remote to be durable and well-made, with buttons that are not too small or too large, and a case that is made of hard plastic."}
