{"input": "Summarize the group discussion about general requirements.", "answers": ["The group had a discussion about the target age group and they agreed to look at 15 to 35 year olds. Also, they decided to make it look simple, but still have those key buttons so it would be easy to use. Lastly, the group agreed to include one sort of menu button and voice recognition as an option."], "length": 8483, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group discussed general requirements for the remote control, including the need for it to be sleek, stylish, and sophisticated, with a focus on simplicity and ease of use. They also considered the importance of a long battery life, a locator feature, and voice recognition, with some members suggesting that voice recognition could be a key differentiator for the product. The group also discussed the target audience, with some members suggesting that the 15-35 age group would be a good target, and others suggesting that the product could appeal to a wider age range. They also touched on the need for the product to be functional, yet beautiful, and to have a unique design that incorporates the company's slogan and color scheme."}
{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["This was a Children, Young People and Education Committee, and it was the scrutiny session with a focus on higher and further education. This whole meeting was conducted in a question and answer format. They firstly started with a question related to the trend of secondary school teachers recruiting situations, and the reasons for this, and the steps they had taken to mitigate this trend. Then they had a discussion on the decision made by the education workforce council not to accredit the University of South Wales with the ability to deliver teacher training. After this, there were some questions and answers related to the reform and reconfiguration of the post-16 education sector, equality of opportunity and university mergers. In addition, the parity of esteem between academic and vocational post-16 education and funding allocation were also discussed. Then they talked about the regional skills partnerships and the pay dispute situation. At last, they shared some opinions on 'legalised cheating'."], "length": 13866, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting of the Children, Young People and Education Committee was held to discuss various topics related to education in Wales, including teacher training, higher and further education, and post-16 education. The committee heard from Cabinet Secretary for Education Kirsty Williams and Minister for Welsh Language and Lifelong Learning Eluned Morgan, who provided updates on initiatives to address teacher shortages, improve Welsh language provision, and increase parity of esteem between academic and vocational education. The committee also discussed the pay dispute in the further education sector, the impact of the £12.5 million reduction in funding for part-time provision, and the development of a new mental health charter for universities. Additionally, the committee touched on issues such as university mergers, the regional skills partnerships, and the use of essay mills."}
{"input": "Summarize the presentation and discussion about the technical design.", "answers": ["Industrial designer introduced the working design including the energy, LED sender, different user interface, and the chipboard with buttons on it. They could put every button under the thumb with an RSI. Then, the group discussed and decided to have removable fronts, a small centralized LCD screen, and a power button with 10 other setting buttons."], "length": 11304, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The presentation and discussion about the technical design of the remote control focused on the basic function of a remote control, which was explained by the Industrial Designer. The discussion centered around the importance of making the remote control user-friendly, with a focus on reducing the risk of R_S_I_ (Remote Control Syndrome) by placing the most frequently used buttons, such as power, channel, and volume, in a central location. The team also discussed the idea of adding a removable front to the remote control, with the User Interface Designer suggesting that it could be customized to include the company's recognition symbol. The Industrial Designer presented a basic design concept, which included a simple shape and a limited number of buttons, and the team discussed the idea of adding an L_C_D_ screen to the remote control. However, the cost of the L_C_D_ screen was a concern, and the team decided to look into it further. The discussion also touched on the idea of speech recognition, but it was deemed too costly and not yet a standard development. The team agreed to focus on the design of the remote control, with the Industrial Designer taking the lead on the technical aspects."}
