{"input": "What did PhD A think about the results?", "answers": ["PhD A thought that most of the nets are not that good, except for the multi English. MSG was not bringing as much information as he thought it would. He explained that even when the features were not normalized, the neural network would perform at 90%, as it would with normalization."], "length": 14016, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "PhD A thought that the results were mixed, with some experiments showing improvement and others not. They noted that the MSG feature did not bring much information and that the combination of PLP and MSG did not improve the results. However, they also observed that the neural network helped to correct some of the problems with poor normalization, and that the TIMIT network was the best performer. PhD A also mentioned that they were still unsure about the language dependency and noise dependency issues, and that more results were needed to fully understand the results."}
{"input": "What did User Interface say about the interface concept design?", "answers": ["User Interface introduced to use the power button to switch the television on and off. The mute button to switch the volume on and off. The channels buttons, one to nine, or zero to nine. The volume and channel quadrants, from left to right, and up and down arrows, to control the volume and channel. And last, the menu button to manipulate the LCD display. User Interface also suggested that power buttons are usually at the top left or right and the team should decide to choose the right icons, or letters on the buttons."], "length": 6032, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "User Interface discussed the interface concept design, mentioning that they would show samples of buttons they had chosen, discuss colors and design, and present their personal preferences. They also mentioned that they had found some interesting samples and examples, and that the buttons should be large and thin, with clear functions. Additionally, they noted that the power button should be at the top, left or right, and that the mute button should be clearly labeled. They also suggested that the menu button should be easy to use and that the icons on the buttons should be clear and not confusing."}
