{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["The whole meeting was about a detailed prototype of the remote control. As before, this meeting also began with personal presentations. The Industrial Design focused on the components of the remote control, including the energy source, the buttons and the materials, while the User Interface suggested to use voice recognition technique and add secured or hidden programming onto the touch screen. Then the problem came that if they would like to make it so complex, they would go beyond the budget and have to raise the cost. Thus they decided to simplify some functions and buttons. Before the meeting ended, they also discussed the shape of the remote control."], "length": 7870, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was a discussion among the project team, consisting of a Project Manager, Marketing, Industrial Designer, and User Interface Designer, to finalize the design and features of a new remote control. They discussed various options, including touch screen technology, voice recognition, and different case materials, and ultimately decided to omit the touch screen in favor of voice recognition. They also discussed the design of the remote control, including its shape, size, and materials, and decided to aim for a non-traditional, sleek design that would appeal to the youth market. The team assigned tasks to each member, including the Industrial Designer to work on the basic look and feel of the design, the User Interface Designer to figure out how to lay out the voice recognition and menu options, and the Marketing team to work on product evaluation and pilots. The next meeting was scheduled for half an hour later to continue working on the prototype."}
{"input": "What did Morneau say about the debt?", "answers": ["Morneau explained that the government was committed to supporting Canadians. It came into the pandemic with a strong fiscal position, and while the pandemic will bring challenges, it will face those challenges while supporting small businesses and Canadians."], "length": 23784, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Morneau stated that the government's approach is to continue making investments to support Canadians, and that these investments are not only supporting Canadians but also supporting businesses to have a strong economy and a strong fiscal position coming out of the crisis. He also mentioned that the government is in a fiscal position that enables it to take on debt at this time, which it thinks is appropriate to get the economy to a better position at the end of the crisis. However, he did not provide a specific answer to questions about the size of the national debt, the total liabilities of the Government of Canada, or the total dollar value of the Government of Canada's assets."}
{"input": "Summarize their discussions on pay dispute situations.", "answers": ["Dawn Bowden proposed the topic of pay dispute and asked what could be done as a Government to try to get parties back round the table and solve this dispute. Eluned Morgan thought this was about ColegauCymru's negotiation, and they were keeping a close eye on this situation. Eluned Morgan thought it would be fair to wait until they get further along down the line. Then Eluned Morgan had a detailed explanation about what they had done, including listening and speaking to ColegauCymru, and they were aware of what the unions were saying as well. Furthermore, Eluned Morgan said they would wish to see pay equality in relation to teaching, but details in relation to this should be waited until the outcome of the negotiations of ColegauCymru. They were aware of all those situations and they knew they were going to have to deal with it in the future."], "length": 13869, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The committee discussed the pay dispute situation in the Further Education (FE) sector, specifically regarding the pay award for FE staff, which is lower than that of schoolteachers. The Cabinet Secretary for Education, Kirsty Williams, emphasized that the Welsh Government is not the employer, but is keeping a close eye on the situation and is aware of the sensitivities involved. The Minister for Children, Older People and Social Care, Eluned Morgan, stated that the Welsh Government is waiting for ColegauCymru to come to a conclusion on the pay award, but acknowledged that the situation is a concern and that the Welsh Government would wish to see pay equality in relation to teaching. The committee also discussed the potential impact of the pay dispute on staff recruitment and retention, and the possibility of the Welsh Government underwriting the costs of a pay award if the UK Government does not provide additional funding."}
{"input": "What did the Project Manager think about their presentation contents when reflecting on their meetings and project progress?", "answers": ["The Project Manager planned to include their project process in the presentation. In addition, he thought it would be an interesting experiment to carry out an open mic presentation in which the team members could get out of the roles and share their satisfaction of the room and their creativity freely."], "length": 9196, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Project Manager reflected on their presentation contents and thought that they had added value to the project by providing a clear and concise overview of the project's progress, but also acknowledged that they had received blank presentation slides from the team, which they had to fill in themselves. They also mentioned that they had edited and added slides to their presentations, unlike some team members who received blank slides."}
{"input": "What did the Industrial Designer and the Project Manager discuss about the LCD screen?", "answers": ["The User Interface Designer thought it might be in the middle of the product because the way users hold the product wouldn't influence the view to the screen, but the Project Manager and the Marketing thought the screen might be covered when held by hands, so the users couldn't figure out what happened on the screen. Then the Project Manager proposed that it was totally unusable, still needing marketing research."], "length": 10673, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Industrial Designer and the Project Manager discussed the placement of the LCD screen on the remote control, with the Project Manager expressing concerns that the screen would be obstructed by the user's hand when holding the device, and the Industrial Designer suggesting that the screen be placed on the upper side of the device to avoid this issue. They also discussed the idea of having the screen on the front of the device, but the Project Manager was skeptical about its usability."}
{"input": "What did the group talk about as their reflection on the meetings and their progress?", "answers": ["The User Interface first pointed out that they did not use the whiteboard at all, neither did they use the pen as well. However, according to Marketing, it was quite understandable that due to the room constraints, such devices were not used. But the worse problem was that they did not receive as many notes as they wanted, the Marketing even received no reply after he wrote his coach."], "length": 9193, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group discussed their satisfaction with the project process, room for creativity, and teamwork, with some members expressing disappointment with the lack of brainstorming and collaboration, as well as the limited availability of colors for design purposes. They also reflected on their roles and how they worked together, with the Project Manager feeling that they had slipped into their roles too easily and the Industrial Designer feeling that the team had been too focused on their individual tasks. Additionally, they discussed the use of technology, such as the digital paper and pen, and how it had affected their productivity and creativity."}
{"input": "Summarize the meeting", "answers": ["The participants went over the results of the most recent experiments, discussing future directions to take. Adding in more languages was still decreasing model performance. The best network consisted of the TIMIT and noise. The team thought that they should try to reduce their dependence on noise in the data. The Professor outlined how they could continue their experimentation."], "length": 14011, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed the progress of a project involving the use of neural networks for speech recognition, specifically the use of multi-stream tandem (MSG) and multi-English (ME) approaches. The team presented their results, which showed that the ME approach performed better than the MSG approach, but that the MSG approach was still useful when combined with other features. The team also discussed the use of different training sets, including TIMIT and multi-English, and the importance of on-line normalization and delta features. They also talked about the need to improve the results of the single-task approach and to address CPU and memory issues. The meeting concluded with a discussion of the next steps, including the integration of the team's approach with the OGI system and the need to focus on the training set and training targets."}
{"input": "What were the three main causes for the financial challenges facing the universities?", "answers": ["Dr David Blaney introduced that the first was the impact of the demographic dip of 18-year-olds and as a result there was an increased pension cost generally. Second, current uncertainty also came as a result of the political environment like the Augar review in England and Brexit. This might deepen the funding gap. Third, due to the political decision to invest in students, universities were faced with challenges of providing more services under limited funding."], "length": 10205, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The three main causes for the financial challenges facing the universities were: 1) the impact of the demographic dip of 18-year-olds, which is deeper and longer in Wales than in the rest of the UK; 2) increased pension costs and other increased costs; and 3) current uncertainty resulting from the Augar review in England and Brexit."}
{"input": "What is Industrial Designer's presentation mainly about?", "answers": ["He talks about something on the components design after having put up the specification properties. As for materials, he used to suggest using hard plastic in order to make the control hard and solid, but at this conference, he thinks that their target audience, young people, love soft colors and materials, like rubber. And he also suggests a shape of a double curved case. As for the buttons, he suggests simple push buttons, without difficult scroll things that makes the control more complex and expensive. And he suggests not using a speaker or a sensor or speech controlled device."], "length": 11172, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Industrial Designer's presentation is mainly about the components design of the remote control, including the materials, shape, and functionality, and how they should be designed to appeal to the target audience of young and dynamic people."}
{"input": "Summarize the meeting", "answers": ["The meeting began with a discussion on the TORRENT project completion being pushed for two years. Grad F then introduced intermediate categorization, which was his topic for his qualification exams. The team then discussed mean subtraction from SRI. Using it had led to an improvement in Meeting Recorder digits though near mic performance worsened. The professor points to pre-echoes as the culprit. The team continued to study differences between SRI and Aurora. The team thought it would be interesting to do the Aurora tests with the SRI system instead of the HTK. The team was also exploring the Wiener filter and VTS. The professor did not seem too excited about the VTS."], "length": 11881, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed various topics related to speech recognition and processing, including the progress of PhD students on their projects, the performance of different speech recognition systems, and the development of new techniques for noise reduction and speech enhancement. The meeting also touched on the topic of VAD (Voice Activity Detection) and its limitations, as well as the potential benefits of combining different noise reduction techniques. Additionally, the meeting covered the use of Wiener filtering and spectral subtraction for noise reduction, and the potential benefits of applying VTS (Vector Taylor Series) in the cepstral domain. The meeting concluded with a discussion on the pros and cons of different noise reduction techniques and the potential for combining them."}
{"input": "Summarize the decision discussion about key remote control concepts.", "answers": ["They decided to implement a LCD display with a scroll wheel. Instead of using hand dynamos, the group decided to use a wind dynamo which was more environmentally friendly. And they would keep the kinetic energy as an option and keep the spongy material preferences as well as voice recognition. At last, groupmates agreed to apply interchangeable cases with incorporated colours to make the remote more trendy. They would use a simple battery, the advanced chip, a curved side case and rubber buttons."], "length": 8979, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed and decided on several key remote control concepts, including the use of an LCD display with a spinning wheel, voice recognition, and a curved, rubber case with push-buttons on the outside. They also decided to use an advanced chip and a simple battery, and to incorporate the company's colors into the design, with bright vegetable colors for the main remote and company colors for the buttons. The team also discussed and ruled out several other options, including hand dynamos, kinetic energy, and solar panels, due to various constraints and practicalities."}
{"input": "What was agreed upon on sample transcripts?", "answers": ["To save time, speaker mn005 will only mark the sample of transcribed data for regions of overlapping speech, as opposed to marking all acoustic events. The digits extraction task will be delegated to whomever is working on acoustics for the Meeting Recorder project."], "length": 19654, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group agreed to use a simple energy detector with a median filter to detect speech onsets and offsets, and then use a cross-correlation filter to clean up the signal and remove bleedthrough."}
{"input": "What was the debate about government giving money to companies which did not put the amount into proper use?", "answers": ["The opposition party claimed that the government had been providing financial support to companies such as Air Canada, which did not pay a single cent in tax nor did it use the money to reimburse customers. The minister explained that the government did not bias against any company, , and it was thought that it was very important to protect employees in every sector of the economy and across Canada.The fight against tax evasion was a priority for the government. The minister promised that they would continue to target companies that use tax evasion schemes."], "length": 20281, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The debate was about the government giving money to companies, including Air Canada, which did not put the amount into proper use, such as reimbursing customers who did not receive the services they paid for. The Bloc Québécois member, Alain Therrien, questioned the Minister of National Revenue, Diane Lebouthillier, about the government's decision to give money to companies that did not use it properly, and the Minister of Finance, Bill Morneau, defended the government's approach, stating that the goal was to protect employees in every sector of the economy."}
