{"input": "Summarize the discussion on improving the back recognizer for the Aurora task", "answers": ["PhD B was conducting an experiment to improve the backend performance of the Aurora recognizer. The goal was recognizing the HTK system by challenging the canonical paradigm."], "length": 8192, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion on improving the back recognizer for the Aurora task centered around PhD B's experiment to optimize the HTK system and compare its performance with the original system. PhD B found that the original system used the same number of states for all models, which may not be optimal for shorter words, and proposed creating more word-specific prototype HMMs to improve performance. He also planned to investigate the expected durations of the models and compare them in the well-matched and unmatched cases. Additionally, PhD B discussed the possibility of reducing the number of states and Gaussians in the models to simplify the system and improve performance, and Hynek suggested that simpler models may be more suitable for real-world applications due to computational limitations."}
